48:            <li><a href="#records">The records</a></li>
56:        <p data-layer="narrative" data-answer="1">On October 2, 2026, G7 leaders agreed to a coordinated release of 100 million barrels through the International Energy Agency over 4 months, "taking into account commitments that have already been fulfilled", with what they called a "frontloaded substantial diesel release within the first 20 days". The same statement says the group will coordinate maintenance schedules across G7 refineries to prevent simultaneous capacity shutdowns. It reaffirms a commitment to refrain from export restrictions on energy and energy products between G7 countries.<Cite s="govuk-g7-statement-2026-10-02" passage="taking into account commitments that have already been fulfilled, we will implement our commitments with a coordinated release through the IEA of 100 million barrels (MB) to begin immediately over 4 months, including a frontloaded substantial diesel release within the first 20 days" /><Cite s="govuk-g7-statement-2026-10-02" passage="We will coordinate maintenance schedules across G7 refineries to prevent simultaneous capacity shutdowns" /><Cite s="govuk-g7-statement-2026-10-02" passage="refrain from export restrictions on energy and energy products between G7 countries" /></p>
57:        <p data-layer="narrative">The French presidency's readout states a ceiling, "jusqu'à 100 millions de barils sous 4 mois", up to 100 million barrels within 4 months. That readout names refined products, notably diesel and crude.<Cite s="elysee-g7-readout-2026-10-02" passage="jusqu'à 100 millions de barils sous 4 mois" /><Cite s="elysee-g7-readout-2026-10-02" passage="notamment de diesel et de pétrole brut, jusqu'à 100 millions de barils sous 4 mois" /></p>
58:        <p data-layer="narrative" data-answer="5">In March, International Energy Agency members pledged 400 million barrels; by October 2 around 325 million had been released, and that day the G7 set 100 million barrels over 4 months without saying how much of it is beyond the March pledge. The October 2 statement asks the agency to "monitor the immediate and full implementation of the March 2026 commitments".<Cite s="doe-spr-release-2026-03-11" passage="coordinated release of 400 million barrels" /><Cite s="iea-g7-meeting-2026-10-02" passage="He noted that around 325 million barrels of the IEA collective action announced on 11 March have so far been released, representing over 80% of the 400 million barrels originally pledged in the action." /><Cite s="govuk-g7-statement-2026-10-02" passage="monitor the immediate and full implementation of the March 2026 commitments" /><Cite s="govuk-g7-statement-2026-10-02" passage="taking into account commitments that have already been fulfilled, we will implement our commitments with a coordinated release through the IEA of 100 million barrels (MB) to begin immediately over 4 months, including a frontloaded substantial diesel release within the first 20 days" /></p>
60:        <p data-layer="narrative" data-answer="4">The IEA's March contributions page says the overall release of emergency stocks will largely consist of crude oil, while in Europe the contributions will primarily take the form of refined oil products. A barrel counted as crude is not the diesel a pump sells. On September 30, Energy Secretary Chris Wright said diesel supplies are "tight" because of export loss related to conflicts in Russia and the Middle East.<Cite s="iea-contributions-2026-03-19" passage="the overall release of emergency stocks will largely consist of crude oil, while in Europe the contributions will primarily take the form of refined oil products" /><Cite s="cnbc-export-ban-2026-09-30" passage={`diesel supplies are "tight" because of export loss related to conflicts in Russia and the Middle East`} /></p>
61:        <p data-layer="narrative">The October 2 statement calls for the immediate and full restoration of navigational rights and principles in the Strait of Hormuz. Negotiations between the United States and Iran to end the war in the Middle East remained at an impasse, and net exports of diesel/gasoil from the Gulf countries averaged 390,000 barrels a day in August, just over a quarter of levels before that war. Combined, net exports of diesel/gasoil exports from the Gulf and Russia in August were 1.6 million barrels a day lower than in February.<Cite s="govuk-g7-statement-2026-10-02" passage="immediate and full restoration of navigational rights and principles in the Strait of Hormuz" /><Cite s="iea-omr-2026-09" passage="averaged 390 kb/d in August, just over a quarter of pre-war levels" /><Cite s="iea-omr-2026-09" passage="negotiations between the United States and Iran to end the war in the Middle East remained at an impasse" /><Cite s="iea-omr-2026-09" passage="Combined, net exports of diesel/gasoil exports from the Gulf and Russia in August were 1.6 mb/d lower than in February" /></p>
63:        <SourcedBlock source="govuk-g7-statement-2026-10-02" kind="record" detail>
66:        <SourcedBlock source="elysee-g7-statement-2026-10-02" kind="record" detail>
67:          <p>The French presidency published the same English statement, including the {release.barrels} barrel release over {release.months} and the diesel release "within the first 20 days."<Cite s="elysee-g7-statement-2026-10-02" passage="frontloaded substantial diesel release within the first 20 days" /></p>
69:        <SourcedBlock source="doe-spr-release-2026-03-11" kind="record" detail>
70:          <p>On March 11, Chris Wright said 32 member nations agreed to a "coordinated release of 400 million barrels," and that the United States would "release 172 million barrels from the Strategic Petroleum Reserve, beginning next week," over "approximately 120 days." He said the United States had arranged to replace the draw with "approximately 200 million barrels within the next year."<Cite s="doe-spr-release-2026-03-11" passage="release 172 million barrels from the Strategic Petroleum Reserve, beginning next week" /><Cite s="cnbc-export-ban-2026-09-30" passage="American refiners are running at record highs" /></p>
72:        <SourcedBlock source="elysee-g7-communique-2026-03-11" kind="record" detail>
73:          <p>The March 11 G7 presidency communique says leaders welcomed the International Energy Agency announcement, prepared at the G7's initiative, "de libérer jusqu’à 400 millions de barils de réserves stratégiques", to release up to 400 million barrels of strategic reserves.<Cite s="elysee-g7-communique-2026-03-11" passage="de libérer jusqu’à 400 millions de barils de réserves stratégiques" /></p>
75:        <SourcedBlock source="iea-g7-meeting-2026-10-02" kind="record" detail>
