143:          <p>From those rows, diesel is {prices.dieselWeekChange} dollars a gallon on the week and {prices.dieselFromMarch} dollars, or {prices.dieselFromMarchPercent} percent, above March 2. Brent is {prices.brentFromFebruary} dollars a barrel above February 27. WTI is {prices.wtiFromFebruary} dollars above February 27.<Cite s="gasdesw-2026-10-03" passage="2026-03-02,3.897" /><Cite s="dcoilbrenteu-2026-10-03" passage="2026-02-27,71.32" /><Cite s="dcoilwtico-2026-10-03" passage="2026-02-27,66.96" /></p>
149:        <SourcedBlock source="doe-spr-exchange-2026-09-29" kind="record" detail>
150:          <p>On September 29 the Energy Department issued a request for an "exchange of up to 40 million barrels of crude oil" from the Strategic Petroleum Reserve. Secretary Chris Wright said several European member countries "have released only a fraction" of what they pledged. The department said five earlier solicitations "collectively awarded more than 133 million barrels," with a "25 percent premium in returned barrels," and that these exchanges will also ensure the reserve continues to be refilled, while saving taxpayers more than $3 billion. Bids are due "October 6, 2026." The oil is to come from Big Hill and Bryan Mound.<Cite s="doe-spr-exchange-2026-09-29" passage="an exchange of up to 40 million barrels of crude oil" /><Cite s="doe-spr-exchange-2026-09-29" passage="collectively awarded more than 133 million barrels" /><Cite s="doe-spr-exchange-2026-09-29" passage="several European member countries have released only a fraction" /></p>
