237:          <p>Javier Blas wrote that asking whether the release includes March barrels that were not released is a red herring, and that the question is whether more barrels reach the market now.<Cite s="blas-red-herring-2026-10-02" passage="It's a red herring: the important question is whether more barrels reach the market now" /></p>
239:        <p data-layer="narrative" data-answer="6" data-absence>The joint statement, the French readout, the IEA's October 2 account, and the Energy Department's September 29 request name no amount of the 100 million that is beyond the March pledge, no diesel-versus-crude split of the October volume, no country share of it, and no October barrel delivered.</p>

