9:“This would just allow them to use that product for more applications,” he says. “It’s not going to save farmers a massive amount of money, but it will provide some critical relief.”
10:Nearly 20 Michigan agricultural organizations are urging Governor Gretchen Whitmer to declare a statewide State of Energy Emergency and allow dyed diesel fuel in highway vehicles registered for agricultural or forest product use for a 90-day period.
11:Missouri and South Dakota are allowing farmers to operate with increased over-the-road weight limits and lifting some dyed diesel restrictions. Ohio is implementing a 90-day state gas and diesel tax suspension.
