6:As to the IEA-coordinated G7 plan to release 100 million barrels of diesel and other oil reserves over the next four months, von der Leyen said the European Union (EU) supported the release, which would strengthen energy security.
7:Hours before the diesel release announcement, the European Commission publicly rejected the possibility of a U.S. ban on diesel exports.
8:"We fully reject any ban on diesel. A ban would not be beneficial to anyone," European Commission spokesperson Anna-Kaisa Itkonen told a press briefing earlier on Friday. "It would undermine our trust in the United States as a reliable partner."
9:Her remarks were made amid questions over reported U.S. pressure on Europe to release oil stocks and the possibility that Washington could restrict diesel exports to Europe.
